Alright, I found the bug. It happens when using "Export selected resources (and dependencies)" and only one file in a given directory is selected.
Here's the MRP: [brokenexport.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/21773204/brokenexport.zip)

To reproduce it:
- open the project so that the editor builds its cache
- close godot
- reopen the project
- select just one of the 2 textures in the assets folder for export
- try to export

I've been debugging like this (on my main project)
```c++
void EditorExportPlatform::_export_find_dependencies(const String &p_path, HashSet<String> &p_paths) {
	if (p_paths.has(p_path)) {
		print_line("_export_find_dependencies returning for ", p_path);
		return;
	}

	if (p_path.is_empty() || p_path == ""){
		print_line("_export_find_dependencies EMPTY");
	}
	p_paths.insert(p_path);

	EditorFileSystemDirectory *dir;
	int file_idx;
	dir = EditorFileSystem::get_singleton()->find_file(p_path, &file_idx);
	if (!dir) {
		return;
	}

	print_line("Finding deps of ", dir->get_name(), "for", p_path);

	Vector<String> deps = dir->get_file_deps(file_idx);

	for (int i = 0; i < deps.size(); i++) {
		_export_find_dependencies(deps[i], p_paths);
	}
}
```

And got this output
```
Exporting  CompressedTexture2DArray res://water/caustic.png
Finding deps of  water for res://water/caustic.png
_export_find_dependencies EMPTY
```

Meaning the problem is most likely this function returning empty strings
https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/de463e0241b0b846fdd3ff76ad12fe6fcf62a9e5/editor/file_system/editor_file_system.cpp#L1858

